window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-a7de5b39bd26a809"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"_1\">浏览器</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> <p><strong>适用界面：cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>浏览器功能在 Codex CLI 或 Codex IDE 扩展中不可用。请打开 ChatGPT 桌面应用，使用内置浏览器。</p> <p>浏览器功能让 ChatGPT 能够打开网站、收集最新信息，并在你掌控的前提下执行操作。你可以用它比较选项、在网站上完成多步骤任务，或检查你正在制作的网页。</p> <p>ChatGPT 网页端和 ChatGPT 桌面应用均提供浏览器功能。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6-astra\">GPT-6 Astra</a> 在视觉判断方面有所提升，适合检查页面是否符合截图，或跨多个网站完成工作流程等任务。如果模型选择器中提供了该模型，可以选择它，并明确说明如何验证任务是否完成。</p> <p>对于受管理的桌面环境，管理员可以限制浏览器可访问的网站来源、上传和下载，以及开发者访问权限。参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=control-browser-and-computer-use\">受管理浏览器控制</a>。</p> <p>请将网页内容视为不可信的上下文。在分享敏感信息或允许 ChatGPT 执行操作前，先检查网站及拟执行的操作。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT 桌面应用的内置浏览器会在对话中为你和 ChatGPT 提供共享的网站或本地 Web 应用视图。你可以用它预览页面、留下视觉反馈，或让 ChatGPT 代表你与网站交互。</p> <p>内置浏览器使用独立于常用浏览器的浏览器配置文件，不会自动共享你原有的标签页或登录会话。任务需要账户时，你可以直接登录。打开 <strong>设置 &gt; 浏览器</strong>，管理浏览器数据以及设备上可用的配置文件导入功能。</p> <p>浏览器下载默认会保存到系统“下载”文件夹。在 <strong>设置 &gt; 浏览器</strong> 中，你可以选择其他下载位置、恢复系统默认位置，或启用 <strong>保存下载前询问位置（Ask where to save downloads）</strong>。</p> <p>当 ChatGPT 需要操作你现有的 Chrome、Edge、Brave、Opera 或 Vivaldi 标签页，或需要使用常用浏览器配置文件时，请改用<a href=\"#/article/a-a7459570776840aa\">浏览器扩展</a>。</p> <p>选择 <strong>New tab（新建标签页）</strong>，然后输入 URL，即可打开内置浏览器。你也可以从聊天中打开 URL，或按 <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>T</kbd>（Windows 和 Linux 上按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>T</kbd>）新建浏览器标签页。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 桌面应用在本地 Web 应用预览中，对浏览器页面上的元素添加了评论</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"arrange-tabs-and-chat\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">整理标签页和聊天</h2> <p>选择 <strong>Enter full view（进入全屏视图）</strong> 可展开当前标签页；选择 <strong>Enter split view（进入分屏视图）</strong> 可让聊天和标签页并排显示。按 <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>B</kbd>（Windows 和 Linux 上按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>B</kbd>），可从全屏视图返回分屏视图，或显示/隐藏聊天旁边的标签页。</p> <h2 id=\"_3\">从地址栏搜索</h2> <p>在内置浏览器的地址栏开始输入，可以搜索浏览历史记录中的页面。选择匹配的页面即可重新打开；如果没有匹配的历史记录，输入搜索词即可使用 Google 搜索。</p> <p>内置浏览器使用独立的配置文件和浏览历史。搜索结果不会自动包含你常用 Chrome 配置文件或其他浏览器里的页面。</p> <h2 id=\"_4\">管理浏览历史</h2> <p>打开 <strong>设置 &gt; 浏览器</strong>，可以搜索内置浏览器的历史记录、重新打开访问过的页面，或在组织策略允许时删除历史记录条目。使用 <strong>清除浏览数据（Clear browsing data）</strong>，可以选择要清除的时间范围和浏览数据类型。</p> <p>如果某项任务需要相关背景，ChatGPT 有时会请求搜索你的浏览历史。允许前请先检查请求内容。浏览历史可能包含内部 URL、搜索词及其他敏感信息；只有当任务确实需要这些上下文时才允许访问。</p> <p><a id=\"browser-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">在浏览器中使用计算机操作</h2> <p>在桌面应用中，计算机操作（Computer Use）功能可让 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 直接操作内置浏览器。所选体验可以打开页面、点击、输入、检查渲染后的状态、截取屏幕截图，并在页面中验证工作结果。</p> <p>内置浏览器属于桌面应用的一部分，会自动安装。你可以在任务中要求 ChatGPT 或 Codex 使用内置浏览器，也可以直接用 <code>@Browser</code> 指定它。</p> <p>例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用浏览器打开 http://localhost:3000/settings，复现页面布局\n问题，并仅修复溢出的控件。\n</code></pre> <p>在 <strong>设置 &gt; 浏览器 &gt; 智能体权限（Agent permissions）</strong> 中，选择浏览、下载和上传的默认权限，并为特定网站添加例外。移除某网站的自定义权限后，该网站会恢复默认权限。你的组织可以限制这些控制项。对于提交信息、购买商品、更改权限或删除数据等敏感操作，ChatGPT 也会在执行前要求确认。ChatGPT 无法通过内置浏览器自动上传文件。</p> <p>网页上的指令可能具有误导性或恶意。允许 ChatGPT 访问某个网站，只表示它可以与该网站交互；这不代表该网站内容可信，也不等于你批准了网站要求的所有操作。</p> <h2 id=\"_6\">预览页面</h2> <ol> <li>在<a href=\"#/article/a-3903992afce071c2\">集成终端</a>中，或使用<a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a?anchor=actions\">本地环境操作</a>，启动应用的开发服务器。</li> <li>点击 URL 或手动导航，打开本地路由、基于文件的页面或公开网页。</li> <li>对照代码差异检查渲染后的页面。</li> <li>在需要修改的元素或区域上添加浏览器评论。</li> <li>请 ChatGPT 处理评论，并保持修改范围明确。</li> </ol> <p>例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">我已在内置浏览器中的定价页面留下评论。请处理移动端\n布局问题，并保持卡片结构不变。\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"_7\">对页面发表评论</h2> <p>如果只有在渲染后的页面中才能看到某个问题，可以使用浏览器评论向 ChatGPT 提供精确反馈。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 内置浏览器工具栏中高亮显示 Annotate 按钮</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>在浏览器工具栏中选择 <strong>Annotate（批注）</strong>，进入 <strong>批注模式（Annotation mode）</strong>。</li> <li>点击一个元素，或拖动鼠标选择一个区域。</li> <li>写下并保存你的评论。</li> <li>在对话中发送消息，请 ChatGPT 处理这些评论。</li> </ol> <p>如果你能明确指出问题和想要的结果，评论会更有帮助：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">这个按钮在移动端会溢出。如果标签能放在一行中，就保持单行，\n否则将标签换行，但不要改变卡片高度。\n</code></pre> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">此工具提示遮住了光标下的数据点。请重新定位工具提示，\n使其始终位于图表边界内。\n</code></pre> <section> <h3 id=\"_8\">样式反馈</h3> <p>为页面某个区块添加批注后，可以在文本输入框旁选择 <strong>调整（Adjust）</strong>，向 ChatGPT 提供更细致的样式反馈。你可以调整字体、字样式、间距和颜色等设置，在页面上预览结果，然后连同更明确的目标一起发送批注。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 桌面应用中，显示内置浏览器批注样式控制的界面</p> </blockquote> </section> <h2 id=\"_9\">控制浏览器任务的范围</h2> <p>每个浏览器任务应足够小，让你能在一次检查中审阅完成结果。</p> <ul> <li>指明页面、路由或 URL。</li> <li>指明你关心的状态，例如加载中、空白、错误或成功。</li> <li>对需要修改的具体元素或区域发表评论。</li> <li>ChatGPT 完成后再次检查页面。</li> <li>打开本地页面前，请 ChatGPT 启动或检查开发服务器。</li> </ul> <p>如果任务涉及代码库修改，请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">审查面板</a>检查修改并留下评论。</p> <section> <h2 id=\"_10\">开发者模式</h2> <p>开发者模式可与 Chrome 中的计算机操作和内置浏览器配合使用。它会向 ChatGPT 提供受控的 Chrome 开发者工具协议（CDP）访问权限。你可以用它分析 JavaScript 性能、检查控制台输出和网络流量、查看 DOM 与应用样式，或诊断实时浏览器中的问题。</p> <p>若要启用此功能，请打开<strong>设置 &gt; 浏览器</strong>（已阻止不安全链接），在 <strong>开发者模式</strong> 下启用 <strong>开放完整 CDP 访问权限（Enable full CDP access）</strong>。如果组织已禁用此设置，你就无法在本地启用它。管理员可以在 <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=pin-feature-flags\"><code>requirements.toml</code></a> 的 <code>[features]</code> 部分将 <code>browser_use_full_cdp_access = false</code> 设为关闭完整 CDP 访问权限，防止用户在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中启用此功能。</p> <p>完整 CDP 访问权限可能暴露浏览器内部的敏感信息。ChatGPT 在使用完整 CDP 检查网站前，会要求你明确批准。批准前请检查网站、任务和所请求的访问权限。</p> <p>使用 <code>@Browser</code> 指定内置浏览器。若要在 Chrome 中使用开发者模式，请先<a href=\"#/article/a-a7459570776840aa\">设置 Chrome 扩展</a>，然后调用 <code>@Chrome</code>。</p> <p>例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">这个应用运行缓慢。使用 @Browser 录制性能跟踪并检查\n网络流量，然后找出性能瓶颈。\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 桌面应用浏览器设置页面，其中已启用完整 CDP 访问权限</p> </blockquote> </section> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-work\">使用 ChatGPT Work 在网页上完成任务</h2> <p>ChatGPT Work 可以跨网站完成任务，包括需要登录的网站。</p> <p>Work 使用运行在独立云端计算机上的自有浏览器，而不是你手机或笔记本电脑上的浏览器。</p> <p>你可以在网页端或移动端启动 ChatGPT Work 任务。即使你离开并关闭电脑，ChatGPT 也可以继续工作。Work 使用云端计算机，在网页上阅读、点击和输入，以完成各种互联网任务。根据请求内容，它可能会使用插件、浏览器，或两者一起使用。</p> <p>例如，ChatGPT 可以帮你：</p> <ul> <li>查找并预约 DMV（机动车管理局）服务。</li> <li>登录水电等公共事业账户并比较套餐。</li> <li>查找并保存符合条件的公寓信息。</li> <li>在社交媒体上研究竞争对手。</li> <li>在会计软件中结账。</li> </ul> <p>你可以控制 ChatGPT 能访问哪些网站。对于预约或付款等重要操作，ChatGPT 会先要求确认。如果 ChatGPT 因任何原因受阻，你可以接管它的电脑，在手机或桌面上亲自完成操作。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT Work 网页或移动端导航到需要身份验证的网站，适用于 Plus 和 Pro 方案。</p> <p>此功能仍在逐步推出。Enterprise 或 Edu 工作区不支持网站登录。</p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-work_1\">ChatGPT Work 使用的计算机</h2> <p>任务需要访问网站时，ChatGPT 会使用自己的浏览器来导航页面、收集信息并在线完成步骤。</p> <p>默认情况下，ChatGPT 在访问新网站前会先征求同意。你可以逐个批准请求，也可以调整设置，让 ChatGPT 自动批准与你的任务相关的网站。对于预约时提交个人信息、付款等重要操作，ChatGPT Work 始终会先要求你确认。</p> <h2 id=\"_11\">登录网站</h2> <p>网站需要登录时，ChatGPT Work 会要求你登录。完成身份验证后，它会继续操作已登录的网站。登录会话会为以后任务保留，因此不必每次重新登录。</p> <h3 id=\"_12\">使用安全登录表单</h3> <p>ChatGPT 看不到你的用户名或密码；模型不会看到这些信息，也不会用它们训练模型。ChatGPT 不会存储你的用户名或密码。你随时可以在 <strong>设置 &gt; 云端浏览器 &gt; 浏览器数据</strong> 中删除所有网站或单个网站的浏览历史记录；删除后，你会退出该网站。</p> <p>遇到登录界面时，ChatGPT 会暂停任务并请你输入登录凭据；如果需要，也会让你输入双重身份验证代码。在 iOS 上，你可以使用受支持的密码管理器顺利登录。</p> <p>请使用 ChatGPT 提供的安全登录表单，不要在聊天中发送密码。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">ChatGPT Work 在 iOS 上暂停 DMV 任务，显示带有网站地址和已遮蔽密码的安全登录表单。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/sign-in.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>ChatGPT Work 在 iOS 上暂停 DMV 任务，显示带有网站地址和已遮蔽密码的安全登录表单。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/sign-in.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <h3 id=\"_13\">直接在网页上登录</h3> <p>如果页面提供此选项，可以选择 <strong>改在网页上登录（Sign in on web page instead）</strong>，直接在云端浏览器中登录。此时任务会暂停。完成后选择 <strong>我已完成（I'm done）</strong>，把控制权交还给 ChatGPT；也可以跳过或取消此次请求。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-browser-task\"></a> <a id=\"start-browser-work\"></a> <a id=\"web-start-browser-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-work_2\">如何开始 ChatGPT Work 任务</h2> <ol> <li>在网页或移动设备上打开 ChatGPT，并在 Work 中启动一个任务。</li> <li>描述你希望 ChatGPT 完成的工作。</li> <li>如果系统提示，请批准网站访问权限。</li> <li>如果网站需要登录，请直接登录。</li> <li>在对话中查看任务进度。</li> <li>审阅结果，并批准任何重要操作。</li> </ol> <p>你不需要单独选择浏览器。ChatGPT 会根据你的请求决定何时使用它。</p> <p>有些网站会阻止访问。如果遇到这种情况，ChatGPT 会告诉你；在可能的情况下，它还会尝试其他方式完成任务。</p> <p><a id=\"website-permissions-and-confirmations\"></a> <a id=\"web-website-permissions-and-confirmations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_14\">安全与用户控制</h2> <p>在 ChatGPT 设置中打开 <strong>云端浏览器（Cloud browser）</strong>，即可管理网站权限。可选项包括：</p> <ul> <li><strong>始终询问（Always ask）</strong>：手动审阅每一次网站访问请求。</li> <li><strong>自动批准（Auto approve）</strong>：ChatGPT 会先判断网站与任务是否相关，再自动批准访问。</li> <li><strong>始终允许（Always allow）</strong>：无需额外审查即可访问网站。此选项可以减少操作步骤，但我们不建议使用。</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">云端浏览器设置显示“始终询问”“自动批准”和“始终允许”网站权限选项。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/website-permissions.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>云端浏览器设置显示“始终询问”“自动批准”和“始终允许”网站权限选项。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/website-permissions.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>你也可以单独允许或屏蔽某些网站，以覆盖默认权限。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT 请你登录某个网站之前，额外的审查模型会检查登录请求及信息的填写位置，查找网络钓鱼或欺骗迹象。我们会测试智能体抵御提示注入、网络钓鱼和非预期操作等风险的能力。</p> <p>为确保操作过程透明，你会看到网站地址和登录表单预览，也可以在继续前检查实时网站。通过安全登录表单输入的凭据会直接传到浏览器，模型看不到这些信息。</p> <p><a id=\"browser-data\"></a> <a id=\"web-browser-data\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_15\">隐私与浏览器数据</h2> <p>ChatGPT Work 的云端计算机与你设备上的浏览器分开运行，并维护独立的 Cookie、浏览器数据和登录会话。ChatGPT 完成任务时所使用的信息遵循你选择的 ChatGPT 数据控制设置。在 ChatGPT 网页端或移动端打开 <strong>设置 &gt; 数据控制</strong>，可以查看这些设置。</p> <p>它不会使用你个人浏览器中已打开的标签页、浏览历史、已保存密码、Cookie、扩展程序或现有登录会话。</p> <p>若要清除浏览器数据，请前往 <strong>设置 &gt; 云端浏览器 &gt; 浏览器数据 &gt; 全部清除（Clear all）</strong>。此操作会让你退出 ChatGPT Work 浏览器中的网站，因此以后需要重新登录。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">云端浏览器设置中的“浏览器数据”部分，以及用于管理已保存 Cookie 的控件。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/browser-data.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>云端浏览器设置中的“浏览器数据”部分，以及用于管理已保存 Cookie 的控件。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/browser-data.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <h2 id=\"_16\">使用限制</h2> <ul> <li>并非每个工作区或逐步推出的版本都支持网站登录。如果任务所需的登录方式不受支持，请自行完成该步骤，或使用其他可用工具。</li> <li>有些网站会屏蔽自动化浏览器或要求完成 CAPTCHA（验证码）。ChatGPT 可能无法操作这些网站。</li> <li>云端浏览功能是否可用，可能取决于你的方案、工作区设置和功能推出情况。除 Free 和 Go 方案外，付费方案可在所有地区使用云端浏览。Enterprise 管理员必须先为工作区启用云端浏览。</li> </ul> <p>即使你的方案支持，功能逐步推出期间，浏览器也可能不会立即出现。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"browser\">Browser</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> <p><strong>Surface: cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Browser isn't available in Codex CLI or the Codex IDE extension. Open the ChatGPT desktop app to use the built-in browser.</p> <p>Browser lets ChatGPT open websites, gather current information, and take action while you stay in control. Use it to compare options, complete a multi-step task on a website, or review a page you're building.</p> <p>Browser is available in ChatGPT on the web and in the ChatGPT desktop app.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6-astra\">GPT-6 Astra</a> improves visual judgment for tasks such as checking a page against a screenshot or completing a workflow across sites. Choose it when available in your model selector, and describe how to verify the finished result.</p> <p>For managed desktop environments, administrators can restrict browser origins, uploads, downloads, and developer access. See <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=control-browser-and-computer-use\">managed browser controls</a>.</p> <p>Treat page content as untrusted context. Review the site and proposed action before sharing sensitive information or allowing ChatGPT to act.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The built-in browser in the ChatGPT desktop app gives you and ChatGPT a shared view of websites and local web apps inside a chat. Use it to preview a page, leave visual feedback, or let ChatGPT interact with a site on your behalf.</p> <p>The built-in browser uses a browser profile that is separate from your regular browser. It doesn't automatically share your existing tabs or browser session. You can sign in directly when a task requires an account. Open <strong>Settings &gt; Browser</strong> to manage browser data and any profile-import features available on your device.</p> <p>Browser downloads go to your system Downloads folder by default. In <strong>Settings &gt; Browser</strong>, you can choose another download location, reset it to the system default, or turn on <strong>Ask where to save downloads</strong>.</p> <p>Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-a7459570776840aa\">browser extension</a> instead when ChatGPT needs to work in an existing Chrome, Edge, Brave, Opera, or Vivaldi tab or use your regular browser profile.</p> <p>Select <strong>New tab</strong>, then enter a URL to open the built-in browser. You can also open a URL from the chat or press <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>T</kbd> (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>T</kbd> on Windows and Linux) to open a browser tab.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT desktop app showing a browser comment on a local web app preview</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"arrange-tabs-and-chat\">Arrange tabs and chat</h2> <p>Select <strong>Enter full view</strong> to expand the current tab, or <strong>Enter split view</strong> to show the chat and tab side by side. Use <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>B</kbd> (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>B</kbd> on Windows and Linux) to return from full view to split view, or to show or hide tabs beside the chat.</p> <h2 id=\"search-from-the-address-bar\">Search from the address bar</h2> <p>Start typing in the built-in browser's address bar to find pages from its browsing history. Select a matching page to reopen it, or enter a search term to search Google when no history result matches.</p> <p>The built-in browser keeps its own profile and browsing history. Results don't automatically include pages from your regular Chrome profile or other browsers.</p> <h2 id=\"manage-browsing-history\">Manage browsing history</h2> <p>Open <strong>Settings &gt; Browser</strong> to search the built-in browser's history, reopen a visited page, or remove history entries when your organization permits it. Use <strong>Clear browsing data</strong> to choose a time range and the types of browsing data you want to remove.</p> <p>When available, ChatGPT can ask to search your browsing history to find a page that matters to the current task. Review the request before allowing access. Browsing history can include internal URLs, search terms, and other sensitive information, so allow it only when the task requires that context.</p> <p><a id=\"browser-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"computer-use-in-the-browser\">Computer Use in the browser</h2> <p>In the desktop app, Computer Use lets ChatGPT Work or Codex operate the built-in browser directly. The selected experience can open pages, click, type, inspect rendered state, take screenshots, and verify the result of its work in the page.</p> <p>Browser is included with the desktop app and installs automatically. Ask ChatGPT or Codex to use the built-in browser in your task, or reference it directly with <code>@Browser</code>.</p> <p>For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the browser to open http://localhost:3000/settings, reproduce the layout\nbug, and fix only the overflowing controls.\n</code></pre> <p>In <strong>Settings &gt; Browser &gt; Agent permissions</strong>, choose default permissions for browsing, downloads, and uploads, and add exceptions for specific websites. Removing a site's custom permissions restores its defaults. Your organization can restrict these controls. ChatGPT also asks for confirmation before sensitive actions such as submitting information, making a purchase, changing permissions, or deleting data. ChatGPT can't automate file uploads in the built-in browser.</p> <p>Instructions on a page can be misleading or malicious. A website permission lets ChatGPT interact with that site; it doesn't make the site's content trustworthy or approve every action.</p> <h2 id=\"preview-a-page\">Preview a page</h2> <ol> <li>Start your app's development server in the <a href=\"#/article/a-3903992afce071c2\">integrated terminal</a> or with a <a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a?anchor=actions\">local environment action</a>.</li> <li>Open the local route, file-backed page, or public page by clicking a URL or navigating manually in the browser.</li> <li>Review the rendered state alongside the code diff.</li> <li>Leave browser comments on the elements or areas that need changes.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to address the comments and keep the scope narrow.</li> </ol> <p>For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">I left comments on the pricing page in the built-in browser. Address the mobile\nlayout issues and keep the card structure unchanged.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"comment-on-the-page\">Comment on the page</h2> <p>When a bug is visible only in the rendered page, use browser comments to give ChatGPT precise feedback.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT's built-in browser toolbar with the Annotate button highlighted</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>Select <strong>Annotate</strong> in the browser toolbar to enter <strong>Annotation mode</strong>.</li> <li>Click an element, or drag to select an area.</li> <li>Write and save your comment.</li> <li>Send a message in the chat asking ChatGPT to address the comments.</li> </ol> <p>Comments work best when you name the problem and the result you want:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">This button overflows on mobile. Keep the label on one line if it fits,\notherwise wrap it without changing the card height.\n</code></pre> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">This tooltip covers the data point under the cursor. Reposition the tooltip so\nit stays inside the chart bounds.\n</code></pre> <section> <h3 id=\"styling-feedback\">Styling feedback</h3> <p>When you add an annotation to a section on the page, select <strong>Adjust</strong> next to the text input to give ChatGPT more granular style feedback. You can change values such as font, text, spacing, and color, preview the result on the page, and then send the annotation with a clearer target.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT desktop app showing built-in browser annotation style controls</p> </blockquote> </section> <h2 id=\"keep-browser-tasks-scoped\">Keep browser tasks scoped</h2> <p>Keep each browser task small enough to review in one pass.</p> <ul> <li>Name the page, route, or URL.</li> <li>Name the state you care about, such as loading, empty, error, or success.</li> <li>Leave comments on the exact elements or areas that need changes.</li> <li>Review the page again after ChatGPT finishes.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to start or check the development server before it opens a local page.</li> </ul> <p>For repository changes, use the <a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">review pane</a> to inspect the changes and leave comments.</p> <section> <h2 id=\"developer-mode\">Developer mode</h2> <p>Developer mode works with Computer Use in Chrome and the built-in browser. It gives ChatGPT controlled access to the Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP). Use it to profile JavaScript, inspect console output and network traffic, examine the DOM and applied styles, or diagnose an issue in the live browser.</p> <p>To enable it, open <strong>Settings &gt; Browser</strong> (blocked unsafe link) and, under <strong>Developer mode</strong>, turn on <strong>Enable full CDP access</strong>. If your organization has disabled this setting, you can't enable it locally. Admins can set <code>browser_use_full_cdp_access = false</code> under <code>[features]</code> in <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=pin-feature-flags\"><code>requirements.toml</code></a> to disable full CDP access and prevent users from enabling the corresponding setting in the ChatGPT desktop app.</p> <p>Full CDP access can expose sensitive browser internals. ChatGPT asks for explicit approval before it uses full CDP to inspect a website. Review the site, task, and requested access before approving it.</p> <p>Use <code>@Browser</code> for the built-in browser. To use Developer mode in Chrome, <a href=\"#/article/a-a7459570776840aa\">set up the Chrome extension</a> and invoke <code>@Chrome</code>.</p> <p>For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">This app is slow. Use @Browser to capture a performance trace and inspect\nnetwork traffic, then identify the bottleneck.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT desktop app Browser settings showing Developer mode with full CDP access enabled</p> </blockquote> </section> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"use-chatgpt-work-to-get-things-done-across-the-web\">Use ChatGPT Work to get things done across the web</h2> <p>ChatGPT Work can complete tasks across websites, including sites where you need to sign in.</p> <p>Work uses its own browser, running on a separate computer in the cloud, not the browser on your phone or laptop.</p> <p>Start a task from ChatGPT Work on web or mobile, and ChatGPT can continue working even if you step away and close your computer. Using its computer, Work can accomplish a wide variety of tasks on the internet by reading, clicking, and typing into web pages. Depending on your request, it may use a plugin, its browser, or both.</p> <p>For example, ChatGPT can help you:</p> <ul> <li>Find and book a DMV appointment.</li> <li>Sign in to your utility account and compare plans.</li> <li>Find and save apartments that match your criteria.</li> <li>Research competitors on social media.</li> <li>Close the books in your accounting software.</li> </ul> <p>You control which websites ChatGPT can access, and it is trained to ask for confirmation before consequential actions, such as completing a booking or payment. If ChatGPT is ever blocked for any reason, you can take over its computer and use it yourself on mobile and desktop.</p> <p>The ability for ChatGPT Work to navigate to websites that need authentication is available on web and mobile on Plus and Pro plans.</p> <p>Availability depends on rollout. Website sign-in isn't available for Enterprise or Edu workspaces.</p> <h2 id=\"how-chatgpt-works-computer-works\">How ChatGPT Work's computer works</h2> <p>When your task requires a website, ChatGPT uses its own browser to navigate pages, gather information, and complete steps online.</p> <p>By default, ChatGPT asks before accessing a new website. You can choose to approve requests individually or adjust your settings to let ChatGPT automatically approve websites relevant to your task. ChatGPT Work will always ask for confirmation before consequential actions, such as submitting your information to book an appointment or completing a payment.</p> <h2 id=\"sign-in-to-a-website\">Sign in to a website</h2> <p>If a website requires you to sign in, ChatGPT Work will ask you to sign in. After you authenticate, it will continue working on the signed-in website. Your session will remain active for future tasks, so you do not need to sign in every time.</p> <h3 id=\"use-the-secure-sign-in-form\">Use the secure sign-in form</h3> <p>ChatGPT cannot see your username or password, and they are never seen by the model or used in model training. ChatGPT does not store your username or passwords. You can delete your browsing history from all sites or one site individually at any time from <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Cloud browser</strong> &gt; <strong>Browser data</strong>, which will log you out from that site.</p> <p>When ChatGPT encounters a login screen, it pauses and asks you to enter your credentials and two-factor authentication codes as needed. On iOS, you can use a supported password manager to sign in seamlessly.</p> <p>Use the sign-in form provided by ChatGPT. Don't send passwords in the chat.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">ChatGPT Work on iOS pausing a DMV task and showing a secure sign-in form with the website address and a masked password. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/sign-in.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>ChatGPT Work on iOS pausing a DMV task and showing a secure sign-in form with the website address and a masked password. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/sign-in.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h3 id=\"sign-in-on-the-web-page\">Sign in on the web page</h3> <p>If offered, select <strong>Sign in on web page instead</strong> to sign in directly in the cloud browser. The task pauses while you sign in. Select <strong>I'm done</strong> to return control to ChatGPT, or skip or cancel the request.</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-browser-task\"></a> <a id=\"start-browser-work\"></a> <a id=\"web-start-browser-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"how-to-get-started-with-a-task-in-chatgpt-work\">How to get started with a task in ChatGPT Work</h2> <ol> <li>Open ChatGPT on web or mobile and start a task in Work.</li> <li>Describe what you want ChatGPT to do.</li> <li>Approve website access if prompted.</li> <li>Sign in directly if a website requires it.</li> <li>Follow the task's progress in the conversation.</li> <li>Review the result and approve any consequential actions.</li> </ol> <p>You don't need to select the browser separately. ChatGPT decides when to use it based on your request.</p> <p>Some websites block access. If that happens, ChatGPT will let you know and, when possible, try another way to complete the task.</p> <p><a id=\"website-permissions-and-confirmations\"></a> <a id=\"web-website-permissions-and-confirmations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"security-and-user-controls\">Security and user controls</h2> <p>In ChatGPT settings, open <strong>Cloud browser</strong> to manage website permissions. Available options include:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Always ask</strong>: Review every website access request manually.</li> <li><strong>Auto approve</strong>: Let ChatGPT automatically approve access after it checks for the relevancy of the website to your task.</li> <li><strong>Always allow</strong>: Allow website access without that additional review step. We offer this option for minimal friction, but do not recommend this option.</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Cloud browser settings showing the Always ask, Auto approve, and Always allow website permission options. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/website-permissions.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Cloud browser settings showing the Always ask, Auto approve, and Always allow website permission options. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/website-permissions.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>You can also allow or block individual websites to override your default permissions.</p> <p>Before ChatGPT asks you to sign in to any website, an additional review model checks the sign-in request and where your information will be entered for signs of phishing or deception. We test the agent against risks including prompt injection, phishing, and unintended actions.</p> <p>For full transparency, you'll see the website's address and a preview of its sign-in form, and you can inspect the live website before continuing. Credentials entered through the secure sign-in form go directly to the browser and are not visible to the model.</p> <p><a id=\"browser-data\"></a> <a id=\"web-browser-data\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"privacy-and-browser-data\">Privacy and browser data</h2> <p>ChatGPT Work's computer runs separately from the browser on your device. It maintains its own cookies, browser data, and signed-in sessions. Information ChatGPT uses while completing a task follows the ChatGPT data-control settings you choose. You can review these in ChatGPT web and mobile under <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Data controls</strong>.</p> <p>It doesn't use your personal browser's open tabs, browsing history, saved passwords, cookies, extensions, or existing signed-in sessions.</p> <p>To clear browser data, go to <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Cloud browser</strong> &gt; <strong>Browser data</strong> &gt; <strong>Clear all</strong>. This signs you out of websites in ChatGPT Work's browser, so you'll need to sign in again for future tasks.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Cloud browser settings with a Browser data section and a Cookies control for managing cookies saved by the cloud browser. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/browser-data.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Cloud browser settings with a Browser data section and a Cookies control for managing cookies saved by the cloud browser. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/cloud-browser-auth/browser-data.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h2 id=\"limitations\">Limitations</h2> <ul> <li>Website sign-in isn't available in every workspace or rollout. If a task requires a sign-in method that isn't supported, complete that step yourself or use another available tool.</li> <li>Some sites block automated browsers or require a CAPTCHA. ChatGPT may not be able to complete a task on those sites.</li> <li>Availability of cloud browsing can depend on your plan, workspace settings, and rollout. Cloud browsing is available in all regions on paid plans other than Free and Go. Enterprise admins must enable cloud browsing for their workspace.</li> </ul> <p>During rollout, the browser might not appear immediately even when your plan supports it.</p>"};
